{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/ds3ipcvy","slide":3,"text":"Feedback turns each failed attempt into a better scoring strategy.","textPreview":"Feedback turns each failed attempt into a better scoring strategy.","textChars":66,"textLines":1,"bbox":[270.01,462.01,739.96,69.96]}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/qpczuhc7","slide":3,"text":"LONG-HORIZON DESIGN PRINCIPLE","textPreview":"LONG-HORIZON DESIGN PRINCIPLE","textChars":29,"textLines":1,"bbox":[410,589.98,459.97,21.96]}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ofy9wn61","slide":3,"text":"0:48–1:06 — But add a coach after every miss—someone who explains how to improve the scoring strategy—and eventually you score. I believe long-horizon agents need that same relationship with failure.\n\n[Sources]\n- User-provided presentation script\n[/Sources]"}
